  "limitations": [
    "Plug-in positive-cohort errors grade marginal forecasts on players who actually played; they are not conditional-on-playing forecasts. Only the Monte Carlo IfPlaying summaries condition the prediction on appearance.",
    "Player pools are reconstructed from earlier box-score listings, not historical pregame roster/transaction or injury snapshots. New arrivals and unlisted players can be missed; coverage and exclusions are reported.",
    "Only players with observed target-game records are graded; missing records are not silently converted into zeroes. Positive-appearance and listed-player cohorts are reported separately.",
    "All-game plug-in calculations are deterministic approximations. The stratified 10,000-draw sample audits the actual final production allocation; its sample size limits conclusions.",
    "Candidate participation probabilities use earlier listed-game frequencies with a fixed Beta(1,1) prior. They are not injury-conditioned, and simulated lineups are conditioned on at least five available players.",
    "Earlier-season chosen player parameters, earlier-season out-of-sample team-score forecasts and a 24-hour results embargo are used. Historical seasons have already been inspected; no untouched accuracy or betting-edge claim follows.",
    "Bootstrap intervals cluster by UTC day; team, player and season dependence can make uncertainty wider. No matched-time bookmaker performance, prop calibration or return evaluation is established."
  ]
